  "text": "Recipe: Jowar Muttige\nCreator: Aishwarya Parasuram\nCategory: Flatbread\nIngredients: garlic cloves, green chili, cumin seeds, water, jowar flour, sorghum flour\nCooking methods: blend, saute, no-cook\nInstructions: SPICE PASTE: Blend together 4 garlic cloves, 2 green chili, 1 Tbsp cumin seeds and a little water till it forms a paste.\nJOWAR MUTTIGE:\n+ Add 0.5 cup boiling water to 1 cup jowar flour (sorghum flour) and knead into dough. While kneading, add room temperature water 1 Tbsp at a time as needed.\n+ Take some dough and flatten into a slightly thick roti using your palm and a flat surface (similar to making jowar roti).\n+ Put roti on heated pan, glaze the top of roti with water as it cooks. After one side is cooked, flip and repeat till roti is properly cooked on both sides.\n+ Remove from pan. Spread spice paste on one surface. Immediately crush it back into a ball while it is still hot.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (sorghum flour), HERBS & SPICES (garlic cloves, green chili, cumin seeds).",
